From e230c5896e144a98c0e2779aef27e96d8ff425c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:52:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 128/130] hydra: computed colour4 alpha, BSDF weight,
 geompropvalue colours

The alpha a separate4 reads is now computed through colour4 nodes: each
one on the way gets a float twin from the MaterialX library - the same
operation on the alphas of its colour4 inputs - a constant gives its
fourth component, combine4 its in4, a converted colour3 an alpha of 1
(K-17).

A pbrlib BSDF's own weight, which no Cycles BSDF has, was dropped: a lobe
at weight 0.5 rendered whole. It is now applied by a multiply after the
BSDF; edited parameters of a node from Hydra are written back, a removed
one blocked (K-88).

geompropvalue of a colour or a vector reads the attribute's colour or
vector output instead of its averaged factor.
